NAME
====

**wattle-deps** - manage the dependencies of a project

SYNOPSIS
========

**wattle deps** _verb_

DESCRIPTION
===========

Manage the dependencies of the project in the current directory. Nothing is
installed under ``*prefix*``. A build made without the OS library does not
include ***deps***, and each verb exits with status 1 after saying so. **d** is
a synonym for ***deps***.

VERBS
=====

- ***vendor***:
  Copy the entries of ``:vendored`` in ``info.edn`` in the current directory
  into the current directory. Each entry is a map with a ``:name`` and a
  ``:url``, which is a source as for ***install*** in `wattle-apps(1)`. It may
  have a ``:ref``, a branch or tag for a Git repository, a ``:prefix``, the
  directory to copy into, which is the current directory by default, and
  ``:paths``, a vector of the paths to copy. A path is a string, or a vector of
  a path in the source and a path under the ``:prefix``. The whole source is
  copied if there is no ``:paths``. A file that is already there is replaced.
  No path may be absolute or contain ``..``. Every entry is checked before any
  is fetched, and no two may have the same ``:name``. ***vendor*** records no
  revision, because the copies belong to the project. See VENDORING in `wattle-applications(7)`.

EXAMPLES
========

Copy the vendored sources that ``info.edn`` lists into the current directory:

````
$ wattle deps vendor
````

SEE ALSO
========

`wattle(1)`, `wattle-apps(1)`, `wattle-applications(7)`
